{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/i1w3yp8f","slide":1,"name":"Oil Slide Title","text":"Oil: A drawn-out crisis keeps crude high and products tight","textPreview":"Oil: A drawn-out crisis keeps crude high and products tight","textChars":59,"textLines":1,"bbox":[28,27,1190,64]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/547294r6","slide":1,"name":"Oil Monthly Summary","text":"• Main message: there is no short-term exit from the crisis. The risk of a sudden escalation has receded, but a drawn-out conflict keeps crude expensive and leaves diesel, jet fuel and gasoline exposed to sharper increases.","textPreview":"• Main message: there is no short-term exit from the crisis. The risk of a sudden escalation has receded, but a drawn-out conflict keeps ...","textChars":223,"textLines":1,"bbox":[46,132,1180,55]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/k3yl0zql","slide":1,"name":"Oil Analysis Bullets","text":"• Political scenario: Renewed hostilities have not materially raised the risk of uncontrolled escalation. Unable to secure a quick outcome, Washington has shifted to economic strangulation; however, China is unlikely to comply and can use rare-earth leverage. Tehran, meanwhile, can wait for a possible US policy shift after the November midterms. With neither side under immediate pressure to compromise, a near-term settlement looks unlikely.\n \n• Product squeeze: In the week to 21 August, NY ULSD traded at 2.02x Brent and US Gulf Coast jet at 1.75x, compared with 1.46x and 1.31x on average in January-February. US distillate and gasoline stocks have fallen 20% and 15% since early January, narrowing the capacity to sustain exports and raising risks for Europe and Asia unless Chinese diesel exports rise.\n \n• Outlook: The most likely scenario is prolonged but contained tension: crude remains high without an extreme spike, while refined products face further upside. Lower US exports would tighten Atlantic and Asian markets. The resulting energy-price pressure would slow disinflation and keep upward pressure on interest rates.","textPreview":"• Political scenario: Renewed hostilities have not materially raised the risk of uncontrolled escalation. Unable to secure a quick outcom...","textChars":1136,"textLines":5,"bbox":[48,205,620,448]}
